PSM2 API Tester
===============

A minimal REST API server that wraps PSM2 messaging operations.  Enables
remote initialization of PSM2 endpoints, tagged send/receive, MQ statistics
retrieval, and graceful shutdown — all via HTTP.

Intended for integration testing and remote orchestration of PSM2 benchmarks
without SSH access to test nodes.

BUILD
-----
Requires libpsm2-devel headers (same as the parent benchmarks).

    cd api_tester && make

USAGE
-----
Start the server on one node:

    ./api_tester -p 8080

ENDPOINTS
---------
    GET  /v1/health     Service liveness check
    GET  /v1/status     PSM2 connection state, role, uptime
    GET  /v1/stats      PSM2 MQ statistics (rx/tx bytes, counts)
    POST /v1/init       Initialize PSM2 (body: {"partner":"host","role":"server"})
    POST /v1/shutdown   Tear down PSM2 endpoint
    POST /v1/send       Send tagged message (body: {"tag":15,"size":64,"rank":0})
    POST /v1/recv       Receive tagged message (body: {"tag":15,"size":64,"rank":0})

EXAMPLE SESSION
---------------
Terminal 1 (server node):

    $ ./api_tester
    PSM2 API Tester v1.0.0 listening on port 8080

Terminal 2 (from any host):

    $ curl http://server:8080/v1/health
    {"ok":true,"service":"psm2-api","version":"1.0.0"}

    $ curl -X POST http://server:8080/v1/init \
        -d '{"partner":"client-host","role":"server"}'
    {"ok":true,"role":"server","partner":"client-host","cpu_freq_ghz":2.10}

    $ curl http://server:8080/v1/stats
    {"ok":true,"rx_user_bytes":0,...}

    $ curl -X POST http://server:8080/v1/shutdown
    {"ok":true,"message":"PSM2 shutdown complete"}

ARGUMENTS
---------
    -p port     HTTP listen port (default 8080)
    -h          Show help
